fwmanager (1.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * A network is also recognised by its router: a copy of a remembered Wi-Fi
    behind another router gets the strict profile, with a notification and a
    Trust button for when the router was really replaced.
  * Export and import of the settings (window and command line).
  * Notifications with the window closed: fwmanager keeps running in the
    background and starts at login (can be turned off in Settings).
  * New languages: Spanish and French, with proper plurals.
  * Documentation in English only.
  * The PPA builds for every Ubuntu release from 24.04 on that is still
    supported, not only 24.04.
  * The whole test suite (ufw, D-Bus, the window, a real install) runs on
    GitHub for every change and before every release.
  * Package scripts use deb-systemd-invoke where they can; lintian is quiet.

 -- Tomascody-web333 <general@homeserverlab.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:23:34 +0000

fwmanager (1.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First release: profiles per network for ufw, a window and a command line,
    changes undone after 30 seconds unless confirmed, Portuguese and English.

